# CODEOWNERS — who must review changes to protected paths.
#
# GitHub auto-requests review from the owner when a PR touches a matching path.
# ENFORCEMENT requires branch protection → "Require review from Code Owners"
# (see docs: repo Settings → Branches → main). Without that, this only *requests*.
#
# Goal for this template: LO authors add their lessons freely (each lesson's
# lo-config/ folder and its media) but cannot silently change the design system,
# config schemas, core engine wiring, the template's own example and shared media,
# or the build/CI/guard setup that keeps every course consistent.

# Everything defaults to the maintainer unless a more specific rule below wins.
*                       @pedbad

# --- Lesson content: NO owner, so a lesson-only PR merges once CI is green ---
# By path AND purpose (TODO §E41): a course's own lessons and their media, one folder
# per lesson, `lo-NN-slug`. Never a whole folder: anything else in lo-config/,
# public/images/ or public/audio/ (a loose file, another subfolder) stays with the
# default owner above. A pattern with no owner after it removes ownership; the
# trailing `/` matches folders only. The table authors read: COURSE_GUIDE.md, "What
# you may edit"; src/docs/codeowners.test.ts holds this file to it.
# Changed here once: course repos inherit this file, so never edit it per course.
/lo-config/lo-*/
/public/images/lo-*/
/public/audio/lo-*/

# --- Template files inside those folders: the maintainer (later lines win) ---
# The example lesson and its media: tests, docs and the showcase read them.
/lo-config/lo-00-example/          @pedbad
/public/images/lo-00-example/      @pedbad
/public/audio/lo-00-example/       @pedbad
# Shared media: the institutional marks, and what the engines and showcase use.
# Owned through `*` already; named so the intent is visible.
/public/images/footer/             @pedbad
/public/images/line-match/         @pedbad
/public/images/placeholders/       @pedbad
/public/images/lo-placeholder.svg  @pedbad
/public/audio/showcase-demo/       @pedbad

# --- Design system: tokens, theme, global CSS (drift here breaks every course) ---
/src/styles/            @pedbad

# --- Config + schemas: the LO/exercise contract and course config ---
/src/config/            @pedbad

# --- Core engine plumbing: registry + shared scaffold (not individual engines) ---
/src/exercises/lazy-registry.ts   @pedbad
/src/exercises/lib/              @pedbad

# --- Build, tooling, CI, and the repo's Claude Code settings ---
/.github/               @pedbad
/vite.config.ts         @pedbad
/package.json           @pedbad
/bun.lock               @pedbad
/tsconfig*.json         @pedbad
/eslint.config.js       @pedbad
/prettier.config.mjs    @pedbad
/stylelint.config.mjs   @pedbad
/.claude/settings.json  @pedbad

# --- Specs + canonical process docs (the source of truth authors build against) ---
/docs/specs/            @pedbad
